    "title": "Emmy Noether: Modern LaTeX Working Corpus and Multilingual Translation Drafts (R804 Integrated Source-Control Head)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21246784",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-07",
    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing Emmy Noether working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. This July 7, 2026 update keeps the compact reader-first layout and adds one current-head package: <code>07_Noether_Current_SourceControl_Integrated_v11_R800_R804_20260707.zip</code>.</p><p><strong>Open first:</strong> <code>00_Noether_German_Cumulative_Working_SourceControl_R796_20260705.pdf</code>, <code>01_Noether_English_Cumulative_Working_Reader_RA10_20260612.pdf</code>, and <code>02_Noether_Standalone_English_Papers_01_43_WorkingDrafts_20260706.zip</code>. For the current German/source-control head after the WebB R800-R804 integration, use <code>07_Noether_Current_SourceControl_Integrated_v11_R800_R804_20260707.zip</code>; inside it the current files are <code>1/01_current/cum_de_R804_integrated_v11.tex</code> and <code>1/01_current/cum_de_R804_integrated_v11.pdf</code>.</p><p><strong>New v11 scope:</strong> v11 integrates source-backed changes from R800-R804: Paper 34 formula-numbering/arrow/spacing and relation-ideal fixes including the carried R799 p684 correction; Paper 40 whole-paper current-head closure with no TeX delta; Paper 14 dense-locus and hazard checks; and Paper 19 p57 varrho-family repair. The v11 package includes the LocalCodex v10-to-v11 diff, copied WebB R800-R804 ledgers/diffs, compile logs, and updated correction/page-QC/hard-math ledgers.</p><p><strong>Earlier July 7 rollup:</strong> <code>06a</code>, <code>06b</code>, and <code>06c</code> preserve the organized R787-R804 source-repair/audit packets; <code>06d</code> is an auxiliary OCR-locator companion. Local intake gaps remain explicit: R790 and R799 standalone ZIPs were not found in the swept Noether folder, although later cumulative material carries the R799 p684 correction into v11.</p><p><strong>Status:</strong> this is a serious source-repair and translation working corpus, not OCR-only, but it is not a critical edition and not a globally certified final Noether corpus. File names inside inherited packets may include <code>COMPLETE</code>; that word indicates that a web-session packet completed its local task, not that the Noether corpus or the relevant paper is certified complete. Dense formulas, tables, scan-difficult passages, and language branches still require source checking. The German/source-control branch remains the authority for downstream translations.</p><p>Older granular repair packets remain preserved in previous Zenodo versions. Corrections can be proposed through the GitHub mirror: <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
